WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.590
- So the impeachment trial is over

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.260
and no witnesses were called.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.900
This is the second time there's been

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.610
an impeachment in the last year

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.440
with no witnesses being called.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.010
But there's several reasons
why the house managers

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.460
might not have wanted to call witnesses.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.560
First of all, Congress says

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.800
they wanna get back to governing.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.930
I think they should be able
to do two things at once.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.360
But, more the point,
they were worried about

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.620
what the witnesses would have said.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.150
Most of the witnesses with
extremely relevant information

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.470
would have been close to the Trump camp

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.200
and who knows what they would have said.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.100
But this is the classic
trial lawyer's dilemma,

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.810
you never know what a witness
is going to say on the stand!

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.010
But you could have ameliorated that

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.010
by taking depositions of those witnesses

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.450
to know ahead of time what
their testimony would be.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:35.610
And while this was unfortunate,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.250
the evidence was overwhelming.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.310
I would have liked to have seen

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.080
more of a factual record with witnesses,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.030
but, look, the evidence was there.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.470
But what do I know? I'm just a lawyer.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.420
And, speaking of which, subscribe
or I'll see you in court.

